  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "ASP.NET Core 11 / .NET 11 GA checked 2026-11-14",
      "items": [
        "HybridCache is the current high-level API for combining local and optional distributed caching, serialization, tag invalidation, and stampede protection. Its package and secondary provider versions are independently versioned; verify exact provider availability for the target framework.",
        "Output caching remains distinct from HTTP response caching: output policies are server-controlled and can invalidate tags, while response caching follows HTTP request and response cache directives.",
        "Output-cache policy API names changed when output caching was introduced in .NET 7: AllowLocking became SetLocking and VaryByRouteValue/VaryByQuery/VaryByHeader became SetVaryByRouteValue/SetVaryByQuery/SetVaryByHeader. Teach the current names and mention the older names only as migration context."
      ],
